ENGAGED. This file ships present so the media-ingest runner is INERT by default
(CLAUDE.md "Autonomous Automation Requires Three Brakes"; DR-0083). While it
exists, run_ingest.sh logs "inert" and exits -- the channel is NOT indexed, no
rows are written, nothing runs. This is the shipped state.

To ARM (Tier C -- Darrell's hand, on an always-on church node, with someone
watching), on that box:
  1. rm state/KILL_SWITCH
  2. touch state/INGEST_ARMED          (enables the run)
  3. touch state/INGEST_COMMIT         (writes to The Word; omit for a dry-run rehearsal)
Then fire it on a cadence (DSM Task Scheduler / cron), e.g. hourly or post-service.
Single-shot + single-flight lock means fires never stack; the 30-min wall-clock
budget (INGEST_TIMEOUT_SEC) kills any overrun.

To DISARM / stop instantly:  touch state/KILL_SWITCH
